  "title": "Marie Curie",
  "summary": "Born Maria Sklodowska in Warsaw in 1867, she studied in Paris, where she and Pierre Curie announced the discovery of polonium and then radium in 1898. She shared the 1903 Nobel Prize in Physics with Pierre Curie and Henri Becquerel and won the 1911 Nobel Prize in Chemistry. She was the first person to receive two Nobel Prizes, and died in 1934.",
